'''''Malcolmia''''' is a genus of flowering plants from the family [[Brassicaceae]]. It includes 11 species native to the [[Mediterranean basin]] (North Africa and southeastern Europe), Western Asia, the Transcaucasus, Central Asia, and Pakistan.<ref name = powo/>

Several species are cultivated for their flowers, including Virginia stock (''[[Malcolmia maritima]]'').

